  "body": {
    "id": "lem:context-construction-soundness",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(s\\in H\\), the mechanically constructed graph \\(G[s]\\) and initialized kernel \\(q_s(v)=p_H(v,s)/p_H(S=s)\\) equal the graph and conditional law obtained by evaluating the known selector gates at \\(s\\).  The ledger base denominator is strictly positive, and no value of \\(S\\) outside \\(H\\) is introduced.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Gplus",
      "H",
      "S",
      "V",
      "pH",
      "GcontextH",
      "laidbackH",
      "seriousH",
      "posLedgerH",
      "Cadm"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:known-selector-gates",
      "ass:exact-selector-support",
      "ass:admissible-cell-interior",
      "def:finite-graph-computations",
      "def:selector-transition",
      "def:step-indexed-ledger",
      "lem:finite-graph-primitives"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "At a selector-controlled vertex \\(X\\), \\(\\textnormal{ass:known-selector-gates}\\) makes its equation the known zero--one multiplexer.  If the intervention-status coordinate at \\(s\\) is one, evaluation replaces the natural row by the point mass at its recorded forced value and deletes every labelled edge disabled by that serious variable.  If the coordinate is zero, the natural row and every edge whose remaining label is satisfied persist.  Erasing satisfied labels and deduplicating does not change adjacency.  Applying this argument once to each finite gate proves that the recursively evaluated structural graph is exactly \\(G[s]\\), and substitution into children proves equality of the induced table.\n\nFor \\(s\\in H\\), exact selector support gives \\(p_H(S=s)>0\\).  More explicitly,\n\\[\n p_H(S=s)=\\sum_{v:(v,s)\\in\\mathcal C_H^{\\mathrm{adm}}(G^{+})}p_H(v,s),\n\\]\nand the sum is nonempty and strictly positive by \\(\\textnormal{ass:admissible-cell-interior}\\).  Division therefore gives the genuine conditional kernel.  Its ledger entry has precisely this cell set and identity.  Since the context enumerator ranges over \\(H\\), no unsupported selector value can occur.",
